Corbell5571 wrote:
>
> Once you got the stuff out of a chest (or a box), is there any reason
> to lug it around? It seriously adds to my burden, and putting things
> into the chest does not seem to ease it.

Putting objects into a chest gives those objects some amount of
protection against monsters picking them up.  Locked or unlocked
few (no?) monsters will remove items from chests or boxes.  Very
few monsters will eat chests or boxes and the ones that do only
digest the chest/box not the items in it.

Many folks use chests in their base camp or cache level for this
reason.  But once you have enough chests at your camp, there is
no longer any purpose beyond pack-ratting.

